  "summary": "Senator Skye Kakoschke-Moore of the Nick Xenophon Team is resigning from the Senate due to her dual British citizenship by descent. She learned this after receiving advice from the UK Home Office and a barrister, despite previously believing she wasn't British. Her mother, born in Singapore (a former British colony), gained UK citizenship, which was then passed on to Kakoschke-Moore. She expressed being 'heartbroken' and 'extremely surprising' by the discovery. Kakoschke-Moore will ask for the matter to be referred to the high court regarding the vacancy, and she intends to run for the NXT again to return to the Senate. A recount might elect Tim Storrer, but Nick Xenophon believes the situation is 'uncharted legal territory' due to a recent high court decision, suggesting a recount might not be the method for filling the position. Xenophon also stated that while he and his colleagues are 'devastated', this is 'not the end of her political career'."
